Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:10:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 26/43] Local (fork-ports2): fork PR #749's view table instead
 of #738's; #738's wave part kept

#738 and #749 both put a table of buffer-view addresses by heap slot on root SRV
252. #749's is kept (16-byte records: address, length, stride; written with the
strides); #738's table, its host code and its view_address change are reverted.
From #738 stay: a mask holding lanes outside EXEC is the lanes' ballot also for
the console's own waves, and that failure retries with the skip widened; a heap
slot the code names outright asks the table too. view_address_indexed lives in
lower_local.rs (lower.rs stays under the asset policy's 512 KiB). Unbuilt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
